{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/33282-101-crossover-story-hooks","id":33282,"title":"101 Crossover Story Hooks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-19T10:14:53-08:00","id":33282,"title":"101 Crossover Story Hooks","content":"1. (Changeling and Werewolf) During a stroll through the dreams of various people in the city, a changeling accidentally went into a Gibbous Moon werewolf's prophetic dream and drastically changed what happened in it. That pack of werewolves is pissed, because that dream can't just be done any old time, and it was the only way they had left to find clues to their new enemy's identity. Luckily, the changeling has friends who can interpret what was seen: a particularly powerful and malevolent True Fae is coming to town, and bringing an army.<br /> <br /> 2. (Vampire and Changeling) Several changelings have gone missing, at the same time that the vampires are noticing an increase in erratic behavior among the Kindred. All evidence points to someone kidnapping changelings and selling access to their blood to the vampires. Years ago, the Prince made a pledge of protection to the changelings' rulers, and when he finds out what will happen to him if he doesn't hold up his end of that pledge he starts to get VERY worried.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T12:00:23-08:00","id":33329,"title":"","content":"3. (Demon and Promethean): Something wrecked a big piece of Infrastructure, and the local Agencies have no clue what the hell did it. It wasn't one of their own, or else someone would be gloating, and it wasn't an intentional demolition by the Machine, because there are Angels on the lookout all over the place. The lone witness is a crazed bum, who swears he saw the building consumed in golden light, and what he swears was an angel. More incidents occur; Infrastructure and Angels both destroyed, always burned, and feverish accounts of golden fire and winged figures. The Divine Fire has come to town.<br /> <br /> 4. (Hunter and Demon): Hunters are going missing all over the place, and nobody seems to know why. Skinchangers would leave bloody messes, Leeches would brag, Witches would be more covert about things... this doesn't fit any of the usual suspects. Everyone from lone cells on the streets to the local VALKYRIE observer is on edge. Something stranger is happening; the missing people are starting to show back up, but they aren't themselves; they have no interest in their former friends, and pursue strange, nonsensical agendas. Where the Hunters are in the dark, the Demons are scared as hell; the Machine is turning lots of people into shoddy Covers very quickly, and they can't figure out what it needs all that manpower for. The local Unchained have a valuable resource in the local Hunters, but one wrong move will have them hunting them instead of their common enemy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 05-10-2016, 03:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T12:45:36-08:00","id":33351,"title":"","content":"5. (Demon and Changeling) Through a Pact, a Demon has obtained the identity of a Fetch. The Changeling has freshly come back, but when it turns out his twin is no longer &quot;just&quot; a puppet but another fugitive, he faces a dilemma. The best solution appears to have the both of them share the same identity alternatively.<br /> <br /> 6. (Demon and Werewolf) A pack's Totem has vanished. Before word could get out and damage the werewolves' reputation, a Demon with the strange ability to make ephemereal Covers proposed the pack to masquerade as their Totem until they got it back or figured out what happened to it. For a hefty price.<br /> <br /> 7. (Demon and Vampire) It's been determined that a ritual that is about to be enacted by the Circle of the Crone or the Lancea Sanctum is no mere ritual, but an occult matrix. It's hard enough stopping human cultists, so just imagine how violently a half-dozen superpowered corpses and their priest(ess) are going to react.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":519,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","user":"ChairKicker","date":". 12-20-2013, 06:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T14:16:42-08:00","id":33397,"title":"","content":"8. (Vampire and Demon): The God-Machine seems to have an odd relationship with time, and often creates bubble realities and splinter timelines. There are persistent rumors that one could lead to a timeline in which the Camarilla never fell and the Kindred still have a glorious, united society. What secrets could these ancients hold for a modern vampire, and why do those who go searching for this splinter seem to meet their Final Deaths so often?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T16:14:14-08:00","id":33500,"title":"","content":"Changeling and Promethean: A buddy-comedy road-trip. A changeling wants to kill his fetch. A Promethean wants to kill his creator. The pair are after the same man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1477-randompaul","name":"Randompaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T22:03:41-08:00","id":33693,"title":"","content":"Mage and Hunter: A new paranormal TV show is looking to film their pilot by looking for a cryptid, only this one is sitting right on top of a powerful and relatively untouched hollow. While hunters would be fine with letting the witches screw this up themselves, the fact is that this TV show also threatens to drag every amateur with a chip on their shoulder and gun in their hand into the area and cause trouble. Either production is sabotaged soon, or both parties are left pointing fingers.<br /> <br /> Werewolf and Changeling: A hunter's gone off the rails now, and they're so insane they've managed to see <i>through</i> the Mask, despite this being all but impossible as far as changelings are concerned. The werewolves are on said hunter's trail, since they're leaving murder and death spirits in their wake so thick that whole blocks are at risk of being urged or ridden. Time to find this lunatic and stop him before he kills both parties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T08:31:14-08:00","id":33883,"title":"","content":"Hunter and Mummy: A local cell is up against something very old and powerful and EVIL. Luckily, an ally at the museum has found someone who fought this thing many centuries ago, who can be awakened to fight alongside the cell. <i>What could possibly go wrong?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T19:28:49-08:00","id":37107,"title":"","content":"Giest and Mummy: A sin eater may have accidentally joined a arisens cults accidentally thinking it was a Krewe what happens when the Sin Eater meets the arisen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T19:57:56-08:00","id":37116,"title":"","content":"14. (Mummy and Demon): Agents of the God-Machine have somehow seized one of the Arisen and have plugged it into a crucial piece of architecture as a sort of occult battery. The Arisen's cult is outraged and panicked, but stand little hope of recovering their leader on their own; the Infrastructure that holds the Mummy prisoner is hidden by other Infrastructure and guarded by stigmatics and Angels. It's a daunting task, but any ring of Unchained willing to take this gamble on has the chance to strike a massive blow against their former master and gain the favor of a powerful being. This could even lead into a shared cult, but there's work to be done before any talk of spoils...<br /> <br /> One of the Arisen is a potent being; it could be fueling a piece of Command &amp; Control Infrastructure. Free it, and the Machine may well lose its grasp over an entire city. That's as close a shot at Hell as any Demon could hope for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T21:08:50-08:00","id":37141,"title":"","content":"15 (Mage and Changeling) A cabal of mages is tracking an odd being, actually a hobgoblin, when they find their way into the Hedge. Lacking much in the way of Fate magic, and any idea of where they've ended up, the nearby Changeling motley needs to decide if they want to help these 'mortals' out before they lose their minds, or draw them further in to make sure they don't go talking about the experience.<br /> <br /> 16 (Werewolf and Mage) Two packmembers have made one of the ultimate sins against their inner harmony, causing the female to become pregnant with a unihar. No rite is known to exist to get rid of such a being before they're born, but rumor has it that they have no such immunities to human magic...<br /> <br /> 17 (Vampire and Mage) Summoning a being from the Primal Wilds is a risky proposition, and sometimes, there's unforeseen side effects; when an Obfuscated vampire witnesses the event, for a brief moment he feels his heart beat, without the flush of Blood within his system. Of course, he needs to learn more about what exactly those magic using mortals did.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T18:27:29-08:00","id":37591,"title":"","content":"18: Hunter and Princess (Unless we can't do fan-splats, in which case I'll edit later): A local nun is found dead in his church, clutching at a small piece of jewelry with a weird emblem on it. Local hunters hear the story and are convinced the poor holy woman just found a bad relic. Then a teen from the same Catholic school the nun taught in is found dead with a similar object in her hand. Hunters think they've uncovered some kind of cult (Or for the Malleus, an infiltration), and are set to root it out. The Radiant are busy too, since a particularly fierce amanojaku killing to keep themselves safe from being returned to their prison. Proactively killing any of the Radiant it can find, the situation and context makes the nakama hunting this killer feel that, sadly, local hunters have started fighting &quot;witches&quot;. If the Radiant can't convince the hunters that they're both after the same goal, the local princesses are facing people who know how to fight dirty in the darkness. The hunters are more curious about this &quot;cult&quot;; Is it friendly, useless, or does something have their eye on local teens?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T23:25:13-08:00","id":37730,"title":"","content":"19. (Hunter and Changeling): Alien abductions. Tons of them. Why are the aliens suddenly so active, and who keeps making the witnesses disappear? The cell comes across an 'escaped abductee,' but can it be trusted?<br /> <br /> 20. (Mage and Demon): The Seers have almost entirely ceased operations in the city. A little digging reveals something far more sinister; they aren't cutting back, they're just <i>gone. </i>The local Pentacle mages shrug, celebrate, and enjoy a break in the competition for a few months. Then a handful of the missing Seers turn back up, but they're acting strange, almost robotic. More worrying than that is a massive surge in Paradox within the city; something is making magic difficult and dangerous, and it's their missing enemies. Is this an elaborate scheme by the servants of the Exarchs, or something much worse?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T08:38:49-08:00","id":81065,"title":"","content":"21. (Mage and Demon) The local demons have been approached by a new ally. It is a strange entity that becomes more powerful as certain pages of paper are gathered in close proximity to each other. With enough pages together, it can disrupt or completely stop the Machine's actions. Through its mortal servants, this entity is able to communicate to the demons. It claims to be an old enemy of the Machine, exiled from the universe and time itself, and it wants to help the demons destroy the Machine so that it can return to reality.<br /> <br /> The entity calls itself the Prince of a Hundred Thousand Leaves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T11:08:10-08:00","id":81674,"title":"","content":"22. (Vampire and Demon) a ring of demons and coterie of vampires are both working overtime to influence and take over a local corporations. When they come into contact with each other, the groups realize that a third party has been pulling their strings. 23. (Everyone!!) A mad seer has been discovered in a local asylum. He/she seems to know everything about everything, but can only access these memories by &quot;flashing&quot; on certain stimuli. This seer is to valuable to kill but no group can allow another to possess him. Even worse, he is actually a paranoid insane person. Each of the characters are members of a group (a krewe, Covenant, Agency whatever) that is tasked with protecting the seer and acting on his visions, defeating the dark things that threaten everyone. When the seer starts having visions of an apocalyptic end, its up to the group to stop the ephemeral enemy. And yes, this is totally a Chuck as a Mad Prophet kind of deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T14:58:45-08:00","id":84232,"title":"","content":"24: (Sin-Eaters/Mage) A group of Mystagouges seek the guidance and assistance of the krewe to either negotiate entrance or be smuggled into a Dead Dominion. They want to ransack a sanctum of a Death Master who lived in their, but his actions long ago caused the Awakened to be barred from entering the Dominion.<br /> <br /> 25: (Mage/Demon) Even Stranger(s on a Train): The local Guardians of the Veil have brokered a deal with the local Agency. The Agency targets and eliminates several high-ranking Seers of the Throne and the Guardians disrupt a major, heavily guarded Occult Matrix in the works, the belief being that each side's enemy won't have the capability of really defending themselves against an outside, unknown threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T15:23:17-08:00","id":84244,"title":"","content":"26 Mage/Prometheans : A young Sleepwalker was found death in his appartement. The scene registers as strange to mages eyes but the can't pinpoint why exactly The only things they are sure is that the corpse was torn apart by spirits. Some days after another Sleepwalker disappears, this time no traces of the body are left. Mages begin to panic as they search for an unseen ennemy as the rare in the know ask themselves why a Created would prey on the Half Awakened.<br /> <br /> 27 Mage/Demon : A group of demons allied with local mages become fascinated with the worldview of the Awakened and try to emulate some entities of the mage cosmology. Some are fascinated by the Arcana and claim they could be the key to the God-Machine destruction or salvation, others turn their look of abyssal entities whose nature is so like their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2225,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","user":"ganonso","date":". 03-04-2014, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T09:30:37-08:00","id":86066,"title":"","content":"28. Werewolf/Geist: The year is 1714. Defending an entire Caribbean island as your territory is a tall order, but it helps that your pack's totem is the spirit of your small ship. And you'll need all the help you can get. Queen Anne's War, as it's known in the New World, has brought unforeseen consequences. All those loyal privateers have been cast aside by the English Crown and now work their bloody trade on anyone they can find. The Shadow was already being overrun by spirits of violence and greed; now the unquiet dead of both the war and the piracy epidemic are causing problems. Luckily, new allies are offering to join your crew. They're experienced sailors who died during the war--and they're uniquely qualified to deal with those unquiet dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T05:23:35-07:00","id":621092,"title":"","content":"29. Hunter and Vampire: The Lancea Ex Sanctum has always been particularly strong in the city. But then the Malleus Maleficarum starts doing a major push into the domain. The Hunters turn their Benedictions upon the vampires, while kindred respond with Theban sorcery. An old time religious war is breaking out in the city. Participate, or get caught in the cross-fire?<br /> +Promethean: Added to the fire are other inhuman beings, seemingly watched over by angels of living flame.<br /> +Mummy: A cult awakens their own prophet/messiah, who unleashed powers straight from the Old Testament upon those who oppose them.<br /> +Demon: Inside one of the cathedrals on the outskirts of town, a congregation has taken to summoning their own deliverance through strange clockwork angels sent by God.<br /> +Geist: Rolling into town is a Krewe that believes Christ was the first Sin-Eater, and is looking to expand their following. It helps that they too can turn water to wine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T03:28:47-07:00","id":670712,"title":"","content":"30) [Changeling &amp; Beast] : A [muggle] friend mentions that someone you both know (but you're not close too) has been suffering from really bad nightmares. Stay home from work for a week bad. When you start looking in to it you find out that 1) it is some kind of supernatural thing &amp; 2) you aren't the only ones looking into this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T09:25:34-07:00","id":671022,"title":"","content":"31.) [Werewolf and Mummy] An rare spiritual event is about to occur, Kamduis-Ur and Anpu are... going on a date! Turns out the two canine death deities have been secretly seeing each other for much of recorded history, but their upcoming date is special for some reason. So mummies and Bone Shadows are being teamed up and sent to acquire various items, spirits, creatures and even people that are somehow important for this romantic encounter and bring them to the location in the physical world that has resonance with both romance and death (such as Savannah GA, Paris France or whichever city of love built on it's dead is convenient for the campaign), where the date is set. However, the Deceived are putting it all on the line to ruin this date, as are the Pure, and the Storm Lords have all been offered a great boon by an overprotective Skolis-Ur if they somehow ruin the date enough to break his little sister and that &quot;Jackal-ass&quot; up. And just why is THIS date so special anyway?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T18:45:50-07:00","id":863417,"title":"","content":"<i><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hihEhsdwiIk\" target=\"_blank\">WIIIIIISE FWOM YOUR GWAAAAVE!</a></i><br /> <br /> 32.) [Genius, Princess, and Leviathan] They've said Walt Disney was a genius. They were right, in a way, he was a Genius. And one who'd secretly inserted Wonders beneath the rides and key locations of Disney World. Their true purpose is unknown, but is suspected to be involved with monitoring children's dreams and cultivating a certain sense of wonder. Baring the occasional Inspired visiting the area to study Walt's work (or for personal reasons), the area is pretty quiet, supernaturally speaking. Some of that may have to do with the Disney Princesses Nakama that set up shop in the Magic Kingdom. But a storm is brewing - a Cohort of Leviathans is planning on conducting a little ritual during the height of the tourist season. One that looks to inflict the full force of their Wake upon all the malleable minds present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T14:10:19-07:00","id":863886,"title":"","content":"33.) [Demon &amp; Beast, though can be mixed with any two other splats] Suddenly, every Hero in the city dropped their quest. Well, maybe not exacly the quest, but all of them, simultaneously, lost their interest in the Begotten, some of them even in the middle of a fight. Similar events happen on the Unchained side of the fence, except instead of Heroes, we have Hunter Angels. A bit after that, they disappear. All of them are gone. With a poof. Then, in terms of the pro-active anti-supernatural instances(Except mundane Hunters), there's a long period of silence. Neither Demons nor Beasts are not bothered by anything for months. And then, after that, they return. But not in the way you expect them. Heroes when confronted with a Beast react with little more than to a normal citizen, but instead, they obsess over another prey. A mechanical one. Similarily all the relentlessness, mechanical precision and others of the Angels is suddenly turned towards the Children. Just what the heck happened here? How can either of the sides survive the meeting with the new threats? Will they reach their arm to the others, even if simply for mutual survival?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T16:31:21-07:00","id":865182,"title":"","content":"34): [Changeling/Demon]: Visit the underpass at midnight on a full moon and spill your blood on an antique florin and it appears to you, an angel straight out of Da Vinci's blueprints - it has wings of stretched fabric and wood, and gears clunk behind a gilded Carnivale mask. They call it The Venetian, and rumors swirl around the freehold as to what exactly it is; an impossibly old changeling, a very odd hob, one of the exiled Gentry, or something even stranger. The Venetian takes parts of people's lives and trades them like trinkets - your face for that of another, your relationship with your daughter for a new ex-wife - in order to let them start over, in order to let them better hide from the Fair Folk. All it costs is your soul.<br /> <br /> 35) [Hunter/Mummy]: You know the monster causes madness in the normal people around it, but you hope your willpower is enough to carry you through to the job's end. As you bury the ancient dagger into the undying thing's flesh, visions flood your mind of people and places long past, speaking tongues long dead... and you realize that you've hunted this creature before, in a life an age ago. It escapes while you're dazed from the flood of memories, but you're filled with new conviction; you /will/ get revenge for the time it killed you in Babylon.<br /> <br /> 36) [Mage/Werewolf]: The wolves are usually seen as a boon to any consilia, provided they don't get in the way too often; the Thyrsus appreciate how they clean up the messes in the spirit realm, and some of them even answer questions when you ask nicely. Which is why it's strange that a young cabal is dead at their claws, stranger than the average murder of the Awakened. The local Forsaken claim ignorance - it was not the work of any of their Tribes, they say - but the spirits whisper about the return of Eater of Names, a totem unknown to the werewolves and the mages alike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 04-14-2016, 04:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T16:44:21-07:00","id":865188,"title":"","content":"[Beast/All]The city is plagued with disaster after disaster. The Birds of Dis haunt the night, a pair of Huntsmen scour the city for victims, a grand host of Bat Shartha lurk under the city, waiting for the next moonless night that they might fly forth and devour, and countless other calamities. All seems hopeless.<br /> <br /> And so the city's Apex, a powerful Beast, has sent missives to the various supernatural factions of the city, calling upon the shadow people to abandon the secrecy and lies so that they might come together and survive. This grand conclave will occur in just a short while, and the players are representatives of their groups called to help ensure it happens. But even discounting those who darkly murmur of traps and cautiousness, getting people to get along is difficult when their ideology is similar; getting, say, the Hunters in Darkness and the Predator Kings to sit down at the same table, much less work together, may be a herculean task. And that's assuming the topics of discussion don't try to crash the party...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T20:57:17-07:00","id":865307,"title":"","content":"38) [Vampire/Mummy]: The Khaibit are a secretive bloodline, largely known for their roles as servants to the powerful; such has been their role since time well beyond the memory of even the most ancient elder. It's because of this that many in the domain grow concerned when a large flock of them appear and beging ruthlessly carving out a niche, destroying local mortal powers in the occult underground and fortifying a new Shadow Cult around them. What has brought them here, and why do they seem so harried? And just what is in that sarcophagus they've brought with them and buried deep beneath that skyscraper downtown?<br /> <br /> 39) [Geist/Mummy]: It isn't just people that leave behind ghosts. What does it look like when a whole civilization is dragged down into the Underworld... and what happens when it tries to come back? The new museum exhibit has powerful and ancient ghosts anchored to the artifacts, mute and devoted utterly to vigilance; the freshly dead are being enslaved in greater numbers than ever before. Every Sin-Eater knows what it's like to come back from the grave, but do they stand a chance against those who can never die?<br /> <br /> 40) [Demon/Mage]: The Ministry of Panopticon has driven all other Seer factions out of the city, and have turned their sights on the local Pentacle mages. Cursory attempts at espionage reveal claims from these Seers that The Eye has blessed them by descending to the Fallen World physically, has sent forth angels to act as weapons and patrons for their pylons. From the shadows come forth unlikely allies; the Unchained, who claim the situation is not what it seems...<br /> <br /> 41) [Werewolf/Mummy, others included]: A bloody turf war has consumed the area, with the chaos spilling out into the daylight streets that threatens to cause mass hysteria. The media spins it as heightened gang activity, but those in the know have caught glimpses of the truth; a splinter group of Bone Shadows who claim allegiance to Kamduis-Ur in the guise of Anubis and a cult dedicated to a Mummy that call themselves the Argent Hand of Osiris. Will you try and broker peace between the two ancient foes, or back one of the factions and hope peace will come with victory?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 05-10-2016, 03:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T21:35:39-07:00","id":865319,"title":"","content":"42) [Beast/All] Tensions rise among the city's supernatural communities when a <a href=\"http://&quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/852386-minor-template-striders\" target=\"_blank\">new group of hunters</a> begin to make their presence known. Before long, a series of attacks have been made. A vampire's elder's Haven is set aflame by a summoned brood of fire spirits, who claim to have been compelled to do so by a potent enchantment. A pack of werewolves are found murdered by the docks, the hunters who killed them easily matching their savagery with ruthless skill. Even the local Consilium was not spared, with many Mages cut down in a surprise attack while they were gathered together. The only lead any of the affected groups have to link the groups together is a Sign marked on many of the victims by these hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 04-14-2016, 04:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T01:44:41-07:00","id":865368,"title":"","content":"43) [Beast/Werewolf] - A sudden and unnatural breakout of Dengue fever coincides with sightings of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/790655-zibhesi-the-red-plague-the-heart-drinkers-the-mosquito-hosts\">Zibhesi</a> by several packs in the area. However, matters take a turn for the worse when a hunt for the Shartha leads to a disastrous confrontation with a massive mosquito monster that they have flocked around as their queen. To make things stranger, a man Ridden by a similar spirit offers his help. He says that the spirit aiding the Red Plague is what remains of his sister, and that killing it will make it easier for the werewolves to dispatch the Zibhesi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T13:24:41-07:00","id":865670,"title":"","content":"44) [Mummy/Vampire] Your cult has woken you with news that they have made contact with an antique dealer with a lead on some artifacts. Unfortunately he seems to know a little more than he should as he will only deal with you directly, asking for you by name. Your memory being what it is, you have no idea who this man is but you do have a general sense that you've seen him before.<br /> <br /> 45) [Hunter/Mummy] The matters of Valkyrie's external funding are a closely guarded secret. Which makes it all the more unusual when an Arisin cult offers to double the Vampire's donations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T20:49:44-07:00","id":883443,"title":"","content":"46) [Any] A Horror of uncommon power is running amok, threatening the whole Masquerade. The supernatural communities open up lines of communication with each other in an attempt to find out what it is. When no one comes up with an answer, a kind of joint task force is put together to dig deeper and find a way to stop the thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T23:35:05-07:00","id":883514,"title":"","content":"47: (Hunter, Genius) So it turns out Tesla was some kind of evil mad scientist, go figure. What's <i>really</i> shocking is that he was hounded at every turn by none other than Thomas Edison. A secret journal of Edison's is rumored to be somewhere in New Jersey, hidden through the decades to keep it away from the wrong hands and eyes. The problem is that there's been activity at the remains of Wardenclyffe Tower, and if something does happen so close to New York City there's no chance of a cover up. Will hunter and genius be able to work together? Will Edison's journal and Tesla's secrets be too valuable to let into the hands of the other? And what would it mean for either group if Edison's journal spread through either community?<br /> * Promethean: More importantly, what does it mean to have more information on the men who were able to harness lightning on an industrial scale? Could this help on the path to the New Dawn? Or be a further detour away from humanity?<br /> <br /> 48: (Hunter: Barrett Commission/TFV, Mage: Adamantine Arrow/Silver Ladder) Recent intelligence has come to our attention that the Marine Corps has been infiltrated, and needs a thorough sweep to remove all dangerous elements. Unfortunately, we can't handle this one on our own. Due to the nature of what's happening, we need to work with another force that knows. Work with them, clear house, and get back any information you have on who these people are and what they're capable of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T18:43:54-07:00","id":884234,"title":"","content":"49: [Hunter/Mummy]: Anyone with a passing knowledge of military terminology is familiar with SIGINT and HUMINT, respectively referring to intelligence gathered from signals and human sources, respectively. Far more obscure is the study of ARCHINT, or actionable military intelligence gathered from archaeological sources. Lawrence of Arabia was a scholar of Middle Eastern antiquities well before he blew up any Ottoman trains, and he represents only the most notable face in a line of Western military authorities fascinated by the secrets of North Africa and the Near East stretching back to Napoleon and even before. It should come as no surprise that the American government has discovered things best left buried in its ongoing overseas conflicts since the First Gulf War (a persistent conspiracy theory claims that Saddam Hussein had a &quot;Babylonian stargate&quot; that gave him power), and specialized teams of combat veterans and embedded scholars have been tasked with investigating all the horrors to rise from the sand. Bedouin tribesmen have always spoke of flesh-eating ghuls and demons of smokeless fire, and it falls to these few VALKYRIE cells to work with the locals to separate myth from bloodthirsty, vicious reality.<br /> <br /> 50 [Mage/Demon]: FOUR FACTS: The Supernal was artificially divided from reality by the Fall. Atlantis was written out of time by the Fall. Demonic Embeds exploit the intrinsic hidden laws of the Fallen World. The God-Machine seems to span the entirety of human existence, and perhaps longer. What does it all mean? The God-Machine is the Lie incarnate, bestowing its utter mastery of the Fallen World to its Angels; it became a permanent fixture of reality at the exact non-moment that Atlantis was removed. As the Inquisitors and the Thearchs compare notes, they begin to shape a vision of Hell-As-Atlantis, and agree that perhaps the destruction of the God-Machine might make the world whole again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 05-07-2016, 12:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T00:42:30-07:00","id":887035,"title":"","content":"51: [Beast/Hunter]: Strangers disturb the Dream, visitors other than mere sleepers. Both are recent to the eternal memories of the Horrors; one is a cadre of men and women in black suits and oxygen masks, government agents and heirs to modern monsters like GRILL FLAME and MKULTRA who use drugs and meditation to perform reconnaissance on the heart of the human race, the other young innovator-terrorists running a hack they claim the Devil gave them in the hopes of bombing the fear and cruelty out of mankind's shared mind. Both are interlopers, and both must be shown their true place in the hierarchy of nightmares.<br /> <br /> (As an addendum, would you like to see these guys written up as Conspiracies?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T04:40:50-07:00","id":887074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/33282-101-crossover-story-hooks?p=887035#post887035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(As an addendum, would you like to see these guys written up as Conspiracies?)</div> </div> </div> </div>But of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T20:41:05-07:00","id":887799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/33282-101-crossover-story-hooks?p=887035#post887035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(As an addendum, would you like to see these guys written up as Conspiracies?)</div> </div> </div> </div> Of course! I'm assuming that <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/33282-101-crossover-story-hooks?p=887035#post887035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the other young innovator-terrorists running a hack they claim the Devil gave them in the hopes of bombing the fear and cruelty out of mankind's shared mind.</div> </div> </div> </div> call their Endowment &quot;Persona&quot; or something like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T13:28:12-07:00","id":889320,"title":"","content":"52: [Beast/GMC and/or Demon] A wandering Beast has brought world of some terrible new development. They were traveling to visit some Family that had dropped out of contact recently in a city nearby. They couldn't find any sign of them in the area, and when they investigated the Primordial Dream, they found strange bits of hardware and cables scattered around their chambers. When they finally get to one of Hearts of the Lairs in the local Hive... the find the Horror covered with machines and parts of its body outright replaced. A flight of Angels prevented further examination, and the Beast fled while their own Kin's Lair started to turn against them. They are asking the group/Brood/Ring for help against this monstrosity from claiming that portion of the Dream - permanently.<br /> <br /> [Explanation: The Rank 5 Angel, ironically/fittingly named Apex is tasked with setting up Infrastructure in the Primordial Dream, which they've done by hijacking the local Beast Hive. They used the 5 dot Influence to Permanently Create the Infrastructure Condition on the Apex Beast, then proceeded to Possess them or use mind-control Numina, depending on what is allowed. They then proceed to repeat the same trick with the other Beasts, delegating subordinate Angels to maintain control over them as needed. Apex has slowly brought in resources and used its Influence to turn many other Chambers into Infrastructure to support other Angels there as it fortifies its position. A small group of Imperatives are changed with keeping any local Heroes out of the Lairs while it works.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T16:14:29-07:00","id":889424,"title":"","content":"[Any] Something's gone terribly wrong. One day, out of the blue, the world shook, a terrible <i>CRACK</i> echoed throughout the city, and the sky shattered, revealing an alien firmament above. Both the mundane and supernatural community panicked, especially when it was discovered the world around the city had become a vast wilderness inhabited by flora and fauna that are very much not native to Earth. The state of the various links to the other worlds would depend on the gamelines be used. But now the city is in chaos, and someone needs to rally the people so they can survive and potentially figure out what's going on. Will you be willing to step up to the plate? Even if it means potentially exposing yourself to the people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T23:37:08-07:00","id":889697,"title":"","content":"54: [Hunter/Changeling; Taking inspiration from the Rose-Bride SAS]: The death of the heir of the Spring Court at her wedding threatens to throw the freehold into a tailspin of war and fighting. No one in the freehold can count on any kind of fair investigation without accusations of corruption and tampering, so a mad solution for a mad people is decided on. A cell of hunters is brought in to solve the mystery. The hunters themselves are concerned that a freehold civil war will result in bad blood being spread around the city, so stamping this brushfire out before it can grow is for the best. Only the courts of the fae are so alien that even a turn of phrase can result in a binding legal contract. Who murdered the bride? Why is everyone itching for war? And can the cell and their motley babysitters figure out just what's happened before everything turns hot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T15:53:05-07:00","id":929429,"title":"","content":"55. [Promethean/Genius]: A group of Botherud, the fanatical Promethean sect that seeks to wipe out their own kind in the belief that Pyros is finite, encountered a Genius who had been using Pyros to fuel his Wonders, and have come to believe that the Inspired are an even greater threat to them than other Prometheans. <br /> <br /> 56. [Geist/Mummy]: A Krewe of Sin-Eaters is secretly contacted by a Mummy's cult. The Mummy in question has started to probe the nature of their condition, and believes that the answers can only be found in the underworld. Their cult has built up a massive store of wealth and resources, and they're offering a substantial prize to a group of afterlife experts who can mount an expedition. Complicating things is that what they have planned would be considered heretical by the wider Arisen community, so the entire expedition has to be conducted with a great deal of care and secrecy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T17:05:39-07:00","id":929457,"title":"","content":"57: (Hunter, Werewolf): It was a long negotiation, but the local pack and cell have come to an agreement. During a major incident, the pack or cell with let two members from the other come along to monitor things to make sure that everything goes right. Unfortunately for the werewolves, they're apparently violating a major part of their kind's laws. A hostile pack is moving in, killing every hunter they find along the way. The werewolves have a choice; fight their own kind, or bow to their laws. The hunters have a different problem. One of their members is a member of a massive conspiracy, and though they've been given clearance to let the cell know that they're a part of something, the possibility of werewolves learning that there are massive organizations like these is too dangerous to allow. Will such a setup be broken because of the actions of a few zealous werewolves?<br /> <br /> 58: (Promethean, Mage: Based off the &quot;To the Flame&quot; SAS): There's been sightings of a bat-like creature at a nearby power plant. Workers are getting spooked, and curious locals are starting to wonder if they shouldn't take matters into their own hands. The regional consilium has sent a cabal to deal with the matter quickly, and locate whatever well of gnosis might have created such a beast. Matters are complicated by the throng of reanimated coming through the area as well, directed by an angelic being to &quot;See and Witness&quot;. The prometheans believe that the creature might be related to what they need to see, and want to protect it.Is the creature some kind of cryptid that the reanimates would be better of just seeing before being sent along? Or are the mages walking right into a Pandoran trap?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T22:59:12-07:00","id":929571,"title":"","content":"59) [Changeling, Mage]<br /> <br /> A reclusive Mastigos has somehow acquired a mystifying artifact; a beautiful moving-illustration storybook that tells simple, (generally) G-rated stories that seem to incorporate random elements from the reader's life, usually including naming the protagonist after the reader (&quot;There once was a blacksmith's son named Jack-&quot;) The book also narrates itself telepathically in a warm, appealing, androgynous voice.<br /> <br /> It would be a simple enough toy, if not for the fact that whatever is in the book, is not just a thinking object. It seems like just a bauble with a tiny adaptive mens slapped in to keep the tales engaging for the kids, but it's not a Mind effect, it's something... unfamiliar.<br /> <br /> The stubborn Mastigos refuses to share their find and finally thinks up a torturous means of communicating with the apparently mindless storybook; they convince themselves for a moment that their name is &quot;Are You There Can You Understand Me&quot; as they open the book.<br /> <br /> The book begins its tale- &quot;Once upon a time, the Queen had a child named <i>Please Help Me Please Please I Hear You</i>-&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 07-11-2016, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T11:33:27-07:00","id":930443,"title":"","content":"Hanging around, trying to build some hooks involving Dragon, Genius, Princess, and Leviathan, but I have to stop to say: Hastur, that is an awesome hook and the thought of discovering such a book gave me chills. I want to be in that campaign, although I realize pretty fast that the book is a Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T11:53:11-07:00","id":930454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/33282-101-crossover-story-hooks?p=930443#post930443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hastur, that is an awesome hook and the thought of discovering such a book gave me chills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, but the inspiration isn't originally mine; I forgot to credit the original idea to Eldan of Giantitp.com<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Apparently a D&amp;D player became convinced that a simple magic storybook they found had a sinister secret, and he tried to investigate it in the most sideways manner, so the DM just rolled with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T23:23:48-07:00","id":931212,"title":"","content":"60: (Historical; Beast/Deviant): The Ancient Greeks fear nothing so much as hubris, the disastrous pride that earns the wrath of Olympus' fickle gods. In the shadows of the city-states, two forces balance the sides of hubris. <br /> <br /> For the children of Echidna, punishing mankind's arrogance is both a divine mission and a source of spiritual sustenance; they are the Furies, and no peasant, king, or poleis is beyond their judgment. They walk the earth openly in a way they cannot in modern time, clad in mantles of fire and trailing destruction in their wake.<br /> <br /> For those who transgress against the divine order (or are just unlucky and caught in the petty feuds of the gods), truly horrendous fates await. Arachne claims to be a more gifted weaver than Athena and is cursed to become a spider monstrosity for her pride, while Medusa becomes a horror after she has the misfortune to be raped by Poseidon in a temple. Whether their current forms are a result of just punishment or unfair cruelty, they struggle against the mad gods and the poleis that have banished them to the wild places of the world.<br /> <br /> What happens when the judges and the judged cross paths? How do the two react when they fine they are kin?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T23:30:50-07:00","id":931214,"title":"","content":"It's not an original idea but thought this would be a fun chronicle. A Hunter the Vigil crossover with....well everything where Task Force Valkyrie puts together a.........Suicide Squad of captured supernaturals. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T00:20:26-07:00","id":931226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/33282-101-crossover-story-hooks?p=931214#post931214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not an original idea but thought this would be a fun chronicle. A Hunter the Vigil crossover with....well everything where Task Force Valkyrie puts together a.........Suicide Squad of captured supernaturals. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I had that idea in a hunter thread. My plan for that idea in a chronicle that I was planning to run was that the supernatural suicide squad was supposed to take down a mortal but supernaturally aware group that was sort of a CofD version of SPECTRE, that was formed when one mortal conspiracy began absorbing the puppet networks of conspiracies that outlived their leaders/purpose (ODESSA, the communist 5th column, various conspiracies dedicated to restoring various royal families that no longer exist to their thrones and a ancient conspiracy dating back to the Antikythera mechanism dedicated to keeping computer technology secret, the Victorian Luddites, that sort of thing) and grew into a vast group whose various branches wouldn't like each other if they knew they were all puppets of the same group.<br /> <br /> I was never actually able to come up with a decent name for the group though. But I still the idea of conspiracies that outlived their purpose is a good idea for a RPG","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T07:22:59-07:00","id":931334,"title":"","content":"61(Hunter/Princess): A cult of Stormswracked mortals are going around to every hunter cell they can find, making an offer of alliance in exchange for territory. Only the big players can turn these cults down, the smaller cells are either bullied into submission or wiped out from the monsters. The few remaining free cells are desperate to end the problem, but that would mean allying with a group of &quot;princesses&quot; with similar powers.<br /> <br /> For their part, the princesses are in a race against time. Intelligence says that forces of Alhambra are on the move to stop what they see as a threat to their power in the region. If the hunters could be turned to fight these threats, perhaps the princesses could stop the Darkness in the city alongside new allies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T07:44:18-07:00","id":931348,"title":"","content":"62) Geist/Vampire: Set about 2007. Hurricane Katrina really shook everything up. There are more Sin-Eaters in the Big Easy than ever, and a lot of powerful Kindred have gone to ground. No one's sure who's got more strength now but some are starting to talk of an all-out war. Even more disturbing, it seems like there are outside forces pulling the strings-- a powerful Krewe from up north that specializes in lowering property values and snapping them up cheap; members of Task Force Valkyrie smuggled in with the National Guard... Can a ragtag group of Vampires and Sin-Eaters keep New Orleans from tearing itself apart before it's even finished rebuilding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T08:00:20-07:00","id":931358,"title":"","content":"63. (Vampire/Geist, potentially Mage and other lines)- The strix population is getting out of control. Just a week ago they were no more than a dozen of them. Now- more than fifty. Their number grows at every night, and their screeches fill the city. The local Lancea, a weakened covenant in the city, claims it to be a sign for God's anger for the sins of the Carthain prince and Acolyte advisers. Some are not so sure- the strix don't seem so interested in tormenting the life of the undead, and they don't stay in the city. They don't come to attack- they escape, with or without a meat suit for the run. That result with an en masses rise of dead bodies, drawing the attention of the local krewes- but it is not their only problem. Apparently, the source of the strix migration is from the local Avernian Gates- each night the doors are forced open from the inside, and a flood of black birds swarm the skies. In fact, you can't open such door to the Underworld without being swarmed by black feathers, as they try to squeeze their way out. When they manage to question a few, all they can gather before to escape is that they are afraid- something drives them from their home, something scary enough to force whole populations through the quickest way out, breaking hundreds of Old Laws on their path and angering every Kereboi they meet. And if the strix are telling the truth, things are going to get a lot worse..<br /> <br /> Apparently, that thing tries to get out, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 07-14-2016, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T18:29:41-07:00","id":931739,"title":"","content":"I gotta add my dragons.<br /> <br /> 64. <b>Hunter / Dragon</b> - A group of Protestant hunters has been receiving advice, blessings, equipment, and coverup help from a local priest, who's been studying the supernatural for a very long time. In particular, he has a strange benediction which causes him to sweat a small amount of blood when in the presence of &quot;demons&quot;. One day, he tells the cell he's found the biggest threat the city has ever known: a newly elected politician is, in fact, a demon, whose true form is that of a dragon. The hunter cell quickly begins to mobilize a concentrated effort to hit the demon hard and fast, warned that if they spend too much time researching the demon, it will catch on and fight back. Some of the members don't believe it's prudent to go after a monster without doing some digging, and find themselves face to face with the &quot;demon&quot;, who tells them some very interesting things about the so-called &quot;priest&quot;, including that he is a 200 year old sorceror who's been running a double life as a reclusive real-estate investor, has been bathing in the blood of the group's kills, and that once he's done with the Dragon, he'll go after the hunters. The hunters begin to question both sides, caught between loyalty to their cell and the potential truth about its benefactor...<br /> <br /> 65. <b>Beast / Dragon</b> - When a particularly stubborn Hero catches onto the existence of the Oroboroi, and manages to slay the eldest of them for their Heart, both groups are suddenly faced with the prospect of a high-hubris Nihilist, whose sole interest seems to be using them as villains in his quest for glory. Can the Oroboroi and Beasts put aside their seething disgust for each other long enough to stop the threat, or will he trample the world in his unending quest for power?<br /> <br /> 66. <b>Dragon / Princess</b> - (from a conversation with King's Raven) When a string of horrific nightmares floods the city, the local Oroboroi den run into a group of Princesses who are battling a mysterious dreamtide entity they call &quot;The Darkness&quot;. When it becomes clear that the entity is working with both a Dream Sorceror lusting for power and a Deep One seeking the destruction of humanity, and that the nightmares are the fallout of this, the obvious alliance becomes the best hope for stopping the Darkness from consuming the city.<br /> <br /> 67. <b>Leviathan</b><b> / </b><b>Vampire / </b><b>Dragon</b> - When the cult of a Leviathan begins to wreak havoc on the city, the Vampire prince sends a group of occult experts to investigate. When the occultists find evidence that the Leviathan has fallen into a deep sleep, and this is the result of it &quot;having a bad dream&quot;, they call in the assistance of the local Oroboroi, who they've known for several decades of their mutual immortal existences. When a trip into the Leviathan's dream reveals a labrynth of personal conflict infested with Nightmares and Shayatin, the entire city may depend on resolving the internal conflicts of the slumbering god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T05:48:45-07:00","id":931945,"title":"","content":"68 (Hunter/Mage): There's an old movie theater, the kind that still has giant neon signs and looks like it was abandoned fifty years ago. Only every second Saturday of the month, the neon flickers to life. People who walk up to the lone ticket booth find themselves staring at a blacked-out window that slips them a ticket for their money. The grime and grit disappear, as old movie posters seemingly appear the second the sun vanishes behind the horizon. Usually it'd just be a fun little urban legend, but now people are coming out changed. They return from these movies wearing old clothes, speaking in archaic slang, with societal attitudes to match.To Mages, this speaks of a powerful combination of Time and Mind magic that must be investigated. For hunters, it means a clear danger to anyone anywhere near the theater. Only the clashing methods of the two spark conflict almost immediately. The Mages want to treat the theater as a well for studying such magics, to look at how it works. The hunters just want to research, contain, and if necessary destroy.<br /> <br /> Fitting that the next movie on the screen when the theater becomes active is &quot;The Devil's Brigade&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T06:59:14-07:00","id":931975,"title":"","content":"69. [Changeling/Mage] The dream called to you, a great Terror pouring of it like a delicious smell... and you were <b>starving</b>, so you disregarded how strange it 'tasted'. After all, Autumn feeds on fear, terror is their sustenance. But, this one had gone <i>wrong</i>. You can't remember what you have seen, just a feeling of all consuming primal fear. And in the land of dreams, in your layer you hear the murmurs and shadows creeping where they should not. What have you stumbled in? <br /> <br /> 70. [Beast/Mage] a madhouse can be a boon for unscrupulous Beast, a banquet of fear, a desirable domain. So, why have this beast become an inmate? Gibbering with fear, with it's layer severed from the Hive.<br /> <br /> [Hint for both, Fangs of Mara]<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T17:26:33-07:00","id":934802,"title":"","content":"71 (Hunter/Changeling): The local community is in an uproar over a civil ordinance banning dancing after a bad accident involving several local teens after a school dance. Everyone thinks it a little extreme, but local changelings and hunters are more suspicious. To the hunters, it might be a sign that a dangerous cult is influencing the local community. To the changeling community, it is an attempt to stifle emotions in the area, possibly to destroy them.<br /> <br /> Suspicion is flying on both sides, and a composite team is quickly organized to bring dancing back for good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T18:40:02-07:00","id":934845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/33282-101-crossover-story-hooks?p=934802#post934802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">71 (Hunter/Changeling): The local community is in an uproar over a civil ordinance banning dancing after a bad accident involving several local teens after a school dance. Everyone thinks it a little extreme, but local changelings and hunters are more suspicious. To the hunters, it might be a sign that a dangerous cult is influencing the local community. To the changeling community, it is an attempt to stifle emotions in the area, possibly to destroy them.<br /> <br /> Suspicion is flying on both sides, and a composite team is quickly organized to bring dancing back for good.</div> </div> </div> </div> 72. And the pastor behind the ordinance is a fire touched Alpha, whose rebellious daughter is an ally to the PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T05:45:45-07:00","id":935009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/33282-101-crossover-story-hooks?p=934802#post934802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">71 (Hunter/Changeling): The local community is in an uproar over a civil ordinance banning dancing after a bad accident involving several local teens after a school dance. Everyone thinks it a little extreme, but local changelings and hunters are more suspicious. To the hunters, it might be a sign that a dangerous cult is influencing the local community. To the changeling community, it is an attempt to stifle emotions in the area, possibly to destroy them.<br /> <br /> Suspicion is flying on both sides, and a composite team is quickly organized to bring dancing back for good.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> NOTE: Must be resolved by dance battle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T10:09:21-07:00","id":937157,"title":"","content":"73.) <b>Princess/Beast:</b> One of the Light, the other of the Dark, Beasts and the Hopeful get along like fire and still-living flesh at their absolute best. Many a Beast and Noble, driven by their hunger and Inner Light, have come into conflict in their mundane lives long before either one realized the other was something more than an ordinary human. This is only complicated by the fact the physical location corresponding to a chamber in a Beast's Lair seems to be a Tainted Location by definition. The two seem made to oppose one another.<br /> <br /> It's a pity your job is to...not so much keep the peace, as to keep the pot from boiling over. Neither side wants all out war (At least, for now), but the inherent interests of Beasts and Princesses are so opposed that what starts as a small conflict may evolve into a bigger one, and the temptation to escalate and call in friends always exists. Your job is to make sure Conflicts between individual Nakama's and Broods <i>stay</i> that way and don't spiral out of control, find common ground where possible, and negotiate tentative peace treaties- or more often, limits on any given conflict. At times, other supernatural creatures- or even the Princesses of Alhambra- are called in as negotiators. Other times, you're working on taking out common enemies. The Nobles have agreed keep those sworn to victory-at-any-price Queen of Storms, or those following victory-at-no-price Queen of Mirrors, from making trouble for the beasts. At the same time, the Beasts are to brook no other creatures of Darkness in their domains- which doesn't always mean to kill them-, and to aid Princesses in banishing the tainted places that often spring up as a result of their activities. You're on hand with both.<br /> <br /> Your last, unoffical mission to get as much information on the other side as possible, and get people in your corner, so when this tense peace does break,your side has the advantage in that conflict. Good luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8045-azunth","name":"Azunth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T13:13:47-07:00","id":937241,"title":"","content":"74 (TFV/Troubadors of Spades) After a &quot;surprise party&quot; for a highly-placed vampire turns out to be an ashen event, TFV is left desperately trying to pick up the pieces. The princesses were easily captured, but the tune quickly changed when the princesses produced documents indicating a possible conspiracy to let the vampires slip their leashes. Time to see what exactly the leeches and their unknown partners are planning. As soon as the princesses stop trying to make themselves look like valkyries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T14:08:43-07:00","id":937275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/33282-101-crossover-story-hooks?p=931739#post931739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">67. <b>Leviathan</b><b> / </b><b>Vampire / </b><b>Dragon</b> - When the cult of a Leviathan begins to wreak havoc on the city, the Vampire prince sends a group of occult experts to investigate. When the occultists find evidence that the Leviathan has fallen into a deep sleep, and this is the result of it &quot;having a bad dream&quot;, they call in the assistance of the local Oroboroi, who they've known for several decades of their mutual immortal existences. When a trip into the Leviathan's dream reveals a labrynth of personal conflict infested with Nightmares and Shayatin, the entire city may depend on resolving the internal conflicts of the slumbering god.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might be interested in <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NuCnt9RB4cugHlQ75cuhN_Pbq6GR_UBNExSaKwsFaIQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. A Leviathan's dreams resemble H.P. Lovecraft's dreamland (because of course they do).<br /> <br /> I'm still not sure how I'll fit that in the book, but even if it doesn't make it in it will be cannon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-25-2016, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T19:23:46-07:00","id":942411,"title":"","content":"<b>75/)(Mummy &amp; Vampire) Forgotten Godhood:</b>The Bak-Ra are beginning to reawaken, and are now desirous to 'recover their lost ability to walk in the sun'. Thanks to the Fog of Eternity, the newly-awakened Bak-Ra have extremely little to go on.<br /> <br /> Then, a Bak-Ra discovers an Arisen and its cult... Mayhem and intrigue ensue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 08-03-2016, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T23:49:41-07:00","id":942538,"title":"","content":"<b>76. Mage &amp; Promethean</b> - There is rumor that Holy Grail of Alchemy - <i>Lapis Philosophorum</i> - is in hands of mismatched beings that ARE living Alchemy. Maybe you found out on of those Created? ( More to read in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/668690-mystery-supernal-alchemy-philosopher-s-stone\">Supernal Alchemy Mystery topic</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T01:06:57-07:00","id":942562,"title":"","content":"To celebrate the imminent release:<br /> <br /> 77) [Mummy/Promethean] When the Mesen-Nebu ended his last Descent, he did so attended by a young brotherhood of scientifically-minded men who styled themselves alchemists. Across the long generations since, they came to covet their patron's immortality and found emulation of his rites lacking, instead turning to hunting the Created for the sweet Pyros resting within them. The mummy at their core was disgusted at first at the corruption of his provided ethos, but has come to view stealing of life and Dedwen from what must surely be considerd the Lifeless. Can the local throng convince a mummy-backed cabal of alchemists from devouring them all? And what strange questions are raised when the Arisen and the Osiran notice their similarities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T16:48:47-07:00","id":943103,"title":"","content":"<b>78/)(Geist &amp; Mummy) Dubious Kinship:</b> A Deceived discovers (or remembers!) the existence of Sin-Eaters and inevitably notes the <i>striking</i> similarity between geists and temakhs. The Deceived puts her cult to use, slowly weaving a trap about a local Sin-Eater krewe. Should she succeed, she perform unspeakable rites to harness Sin-Eater magic for herself!<br /> <br /> (Of course, this attempt, canonically speaking, is doomed to failure, but the Deceived doesn't know that...much to the horror of the krewe!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T09:31:01-07:00","id":946221,"title":"","content":"<b>79) [Demon &amp; Princess]</b> <i>The Story Hook exists in multiple phases, each representing the plot moved further along in its operation, or an optional complication.</i><br /> <br /> \u2022 The callous workings of the God-Machine have inadvertently strengthened the Darkness in the area, leading to an abnormally high number of Tainted areas, and swarms of Darkened and Darkspawn. These creatures risked contamination of other Projects' Outputs, and so had to be contained. It determined the best way to do this would be to hook up Princesses into Infrastructure that would use their Inner Light to suppress the Tainted connections to the Dark World, and drive out the Darkened. The Ring must work with local Nakamas to protect them from the Machine's agents (and earn their trust enough to do so).<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022 When the Ring uncovers this piece of Infrastructure, they learn that even if they kill the entrapped Princesses, <i>another</i> piece of Infrastructure is set up to entrap their souls instead of letting them reincarnate (the backup Infrastructure isn't as efficient, so keeping the captive Nobles alive is still desirable). They'll need to co-ordinate with a Nakama to hit both sites simultaneously, or risk the hit on one alerting the other.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Servants of the Darkness have learned of this Soul-Entrapment device, and seek to steal it to fortify and repair the imprisoning powers of the Dreamworld.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Another Ring has contacted a different Nakama, but sources indicate they are going to betray them and instead Suborn the Infrastructure to their own purposes (Or, this could be the PC Ring's goal). Not only is this interference, but if the information leaks, it could threaten the already tenuous ties of trust.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Stormwracked were contacted by agent of the God-Machine, and offered assistance against the forces of the Darkness in exchange for selling out Unchained to be captured. They've already led one Ring to capture and recycling, and if/when word spreads, it could bring down what fragile alliance exist between Princess and Demon.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 The Infrastructure lies in ruins and the souls of the entrapped Nobles released to be reincarnated. But that leaves the Darkness completely unopposed, and swarms of Darkspawn, Mnemosyn, Cataphractoi, and Darkened Cryptids to plague the area. They need to be put in check the hard way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T10:00:06-07:00","id":946242,"title":"","content":"<b>80) [Demon &amp; Promethean 2E]</b> A new Alchemist corporation is boast of having found a way to &quot;stabilize&quot; Pyros, leading to workings that require no additional input (or risk madness), though they are not as potent as more &quot;traditional&quot; methods. A bidding and corporate espionage war has started of large organizations trying to steal this upstart's secrets. They don't know that the reason given is BS - their &quot;concoctions&quot; are actually Show of Power Gadgets based on true Distillations. Why the controlling Demons are playing this game and what they hope to gain is a mystery. As is what would happen when you pour <i>actual</i> Pyros into these knockoffs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T11:08:55-07:00","id":946295,"title":"","content":"(Geist and Changeling) A new designer drug is making its run through the city club scene. A powerful hallucinogen and stimulant it guarantees a good night, unless the images you see makes your heart stop or you become so stimulated you forget how to feel pain, or your dehydrate. A local Krewe begins searching for the source of this drug because the spirits it creates are unusually disruptive and powerful. Their path leads them to motley that is selling a goblin fruit found in the hedge, which they dry and cut into powder and sell as a drug. Are these Changelings alone in this or is the whole freehold involved? Can other motley's help them take down this dangerous ring before more people die?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2015-inspectorjavert","name":"inspectorjavert","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:35:33-07:00","id":947014,"title":"","content":"82. <b>(Any and Vampire):</b> There's a Dragon coming to town, and this Dragon collects an unusual hoard. The Hydra, her real name long since forgotten, is a bogeyman among bogeymen, a rogue member of the Ordo Dracul who developed the Coil of Zirnitra to mastery- some say she even created it. After developing the power to Graft Unholy Flesh, she became obsessed with &quot;collecting&quot; powers from other supernatural beings. The lure that brings her to town is the presence of a rare monster that she's been searching for, such as a Demon, a Promethean, or an Azlu Crone. The Hydra will stop at nothing to win her bounty, and her arsenal of stolen powers makes her a terrifying foe, especially as she's adept at using Obfuscate and Protean to hide the many extra limbs and appendages that sprout from her body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T13:10:38-07:00","id":947986,"title":"","content":"<b>83/)(Changeling/Geist) The Plaguedog:</b> A krewe of Sin-Eaters have begun investigating a string of mysterious deaths: human beings, riddled with disease, dead from <i>explosive</i> tumor-growth. They think an Abmortal is responsible, but the truth is weirder: a dual-kith'd Darkling Gravewight/Roteater, a 'hyena' thrumming with hundreds of different diseases, being a Typhoid carrier for nearly ALL of them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T16:58:47-07:00","id":948176,"title":"","content":"<b>84/)(Beast &amp; Changeling) The Pack:</b> A Begotten Eshmaki with the Fenris wolf as her Horror has formed a Kinship with Briarwolves from the Hedge, thanks to the Beast stumbling across a trod she somehow was able to open. Of course, these Briarwolves are a 'hunting pack' loyal to the Lion of Sun and Bonze and Blood, a particularly feral Keeper. Thanks to this, a <i>Gentry</i> has become the area's Apex!<br /> <br /> The Primordial Dream in the region will <i>never</i> be the same, again!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T15:24:57-07:00","id":949570,"title":"","content":"<b>85. (Mage: The Transgression and Demon):</b> An Unchained is convinced that Bardos are their best bet of creating a personal Hell, but they have to deal with the fact that the Machine has ways of attacking and co-opting them. So they're enlisting any Mages interested to help them look for a way to move a Bardo off the Machine's radar...before it finds out what they're trying to do and sends an angelic host after them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 08-12-2016, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T15:38:01-07:00","id":949578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/33282-101-crossover-story-hooks?p=949570#post949570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>85. (Mage and Demon):</b> An Unchained is convinced that Bardos are their best bet of creating a personal Hell, but they have to deal with the fact that the Machine has ways of attacking and co-opting them. So they're enlisting any Mages interested to help them look for a way to move a Bardo off the Machine's radar...before it finds out what they're trying to do and sends an angelic host after them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bardos are Genius material, not Mage. I know from context that you are referring to your own hybrid take on Mage and Genius, but you should probably explicitly list that to prevent confusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T17:09:02-07:00","id":949645,"title":"","content":"<b>86- Essence of the Wolf [Promethean/Werewolf]:</b> There's been a uproar amongst the local Uratha. For most, the death by disection of a homeless person might not ping too many radars, but the fact that this individual reeked of Essence was something the Aspirants of the Lodge of the Shield thought worth looking into. Unfortunately, they were forced to put it on hold when the first Werewolf died. Since then, two others have been picked off, all killed and then mutilated in the same ritualistic way. Already, the Rahu and Elodoth sharpen their claws as they wonder when this shadow killer will next strike.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, a Throng of Prometheans watch worriedly over recent events. An Ulgan they had just met has been killed in a way that implies more than mere malice, and now a number of unconnected individuals has been murdered, their bodies devoid of the organs and fluids associated with the classical humors. Besides the fact that Disquiet risks making them subjects #1, a stranger appears to be stalking them, and it appears they could very well be the next victims.<br /> <br /> In truth, the blame for the murders lie at the feet of an Alchemist, one grown twisted and jealous after watching his brother undergo the First Change while he remained mortal. He believes he can use Vitriol mixed with the humors of a Werewolf will allow him to force his way into the People; so far he has managed to force himself to manifest a Tell, and now he hopes to expand even further. Will the Forsaken and the Created be able to put aside the things that keep them apart before someone else dies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T17:37:07-07:00","id":949655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/33282-101-crossover-story-hooks?p=949645#post949645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>86- Essence of the Wolf [Promethean/Werewolf]:</b> There's been a uproar amongst the local Uratha. For most, the death by disection of a homeless person might not ping too many radars, but the fact that this individual reeked of Essence was something the Aspirants of the Lodge of the Shield thought worth looking into. Unfortunately, they were forced to put it on hold when the first Werewolf died. Since then, two others have been picked off, all killed and then mutilated in the same ritualistic way. Already, the Rahu and Elodoth sharpen their claws as they wonder when this shadow killer will next strike.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, a Throng of Prometheans watch worriedly over recent events. An Ulgan they had just met has been killed in a way that implies more than mere malice, and now a number of unconnected individuals has been murdered, their bodies devoid of the organs and fluids associated with the classical humors. Besides the fact that Disquiet risks making them subjects #1, a stranger appears to be stalking them, and it appears they could very well be the next victims.<br /> <br /> In truth, the blame for the murders lie at the feet of an Alchemist, one grown twisted and jealous after watching his brother undergo the First Change while he remained mortal. He believes he can use Vitriol mixed with the humors of a Werewolf will allow him to force his way into the People; so far he has managed to force himself to manifest a Tell, and now he hopes to expand even further. Will the Forsaken and the Created be able to put aside the things that keep them apart before someone else dies?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is awesome! However...are Alchemists something out of PtC 2e? I only have <i>Promethean: The Created</i> 1st Edition, so... Yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T18:58:05-07:00","id":949692,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3514\" data-vbnamecard=\"3514\">ZealousChristian24</a>, here's an extension to your story hook from my end. <hr /><br /> <u><b>Hunt of the Ember Wolves</b></u><br /> Matters get more complicated when adherents from the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/946171-lodge-of-the-splintered-tree-2e#post946171\">Lodge of the Splintered Tree</a> involve themselves in the situation. They have picked up the signs that several Prometheans are in the area, and recognize the harvested organs and fluids as being associated with alchemic humours. Unfortunately, they make the assumption that some of their prey have a hand in the murders, and prepare themselves to declare <i>Siskur-Dah</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 08-13-2016, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T19:40:17-07:00","id":949724,"title":"","content":"<b>87/) (Promethean and Geist) Shaman War:</b> An Ulgan made from a statue of some famous mortal person has begun corralling ghosts under his 'control', not realizing his 'mastery' is a thin sham. A local Sin-Eater krewe (the PCs!) has become aware of the gathering ghost horde. Can they do something, or will the Ulgan unleash something horrific in his folly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T20:18:09-07:00","id":949761,"title":"","content":"<b>88. Changeling and Promethean:</b> A True Fae who fancies himself an artist of Fetches has found out about the Created, and he's getting a bit jealous. Not only can these beings do things that not even his &quot;masterpieces&quot; can, but they can apparently be made by mere mortals! The Sculptor of Leaves is obviously quite curious, and he's looking for any leads on how to incorporate Pyros into his creations. Making things more dangerous, a Promethean who wishes to become a True Fae has fallen under his sway in the search of their New Dawn, and is providing the Sculptor with knowledge and resources...and test subjects. <br /> <br /> <b>89. Promethean and Mage: The Transgression:</b> An Abyssal Disassociation has formed that seems to have its sights set on wiping out the Created. The rapid growth of this entity is suspicious, and it turns out that the Redeemers, a cult of Prometheans that believe that their own kind are abominations, have been &quot;feeding&quot; it and helping it grow. But any Mages who investigate might wonder how they gained so much knowledge about the Abyss- do they have a benefactor within the Mage community?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T12:35:30-07:00","id":995750,"title":"","content":"90 (Promethean/Mage): She didn't exist a week ago; now, she's standing on a downtown street corner speaking gibberish gospel to mostly-indifferent crowds walking by. The rare few that listen have their eyes ripped open to the symbols of the Supernal, their minds cracking in the face of truths only an Awakened soul can comprehend. Where did she come from? How is she doing this? Why is her skin covered in tattoos that look so much like High Speech?<br /> <br /> 91 (Vampire/Demon): When a neonate goes missing, few care to make note of it; they assume her nerve failed her and she faced the sun, or that her indiscretions led to an early Final Death at the hands of hunters or rivals. It's when she shows up on security camera footage two weeks later, killing a gas station clerk with new syringe-fingers, that the undead start to ask questions. Other young Kindred have gone missing as well, and now no one can find the leader of the local Crone cult...<br /> <br /> 92 (Beast/Changeling/Mage): A new indie film has just hit local theaters after receiving high praise at a small film festival, and seems to be a triumph of low-budget horror that uses strikingly hand-painted sets and minimal dialogue to convey its moods and themes. Critics and aficionados are riveted by the distinct, surreal visuals... riveted enough that the dreams of the entire city are taking on a sinister, cinematic quality. The images of the film are bleeding into the minds of people who have never seen or even heard of the film, and some have claimed to see its nameless stars in places where the membrane between worlds grows thin. And now the director seems to have vanished, and nobody seems to recall their name, or indeed even what they looked like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T01:04:46-07:00","id":995994,"title":"","content":"Totally stealing number 90 for my <b>Mage / Promethean </b>crossover. We even started with new Golem covered in tattoos in image of Kabbalah's Tree of Life! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T07:05:27-07:00","id":996056,"title":"","content":"Hunter (Malleus Maleficarum) / Leviathan.<br /> <br /> Something has happened in the heavens. Prayers are going unanswered and you feel a gaping void in your soul. Soon the very rules of reality are falling apart. First the more complex ones like Love, but even simpler things like the whether are starting to fall apart.<br /> <br /> But some trace of divinity remains. The Tribe are thriving. Mankind flocks to their cults in droves to fill the void in their souls with the Wake and the hole in their bellies with the bounty of the seas (it seems the Vestige of Elements isn't falling apart with the rest of the weather).<br /> <br /> Somebody needs to fill the empty thrones in the heavens, and there are no good candidates left. Can the church mentor Leviathans so that they may lead this world, can Christianity create a new theology that embraces man's darkest natures and turns them to good ends?<br /> <br /> Or is such a thing too horrible to contemplate? Will the church stand for it's principals and reject mankind's demons even as the very world falls apart? Fiat justitia ruat c\u00e6lum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T08:14:18-07:00","id":996079,"title":"","content":"95)<b>Deviant/Princess:</b>An urban legend appears among the Nobles of a city. Someone that looks like the best version of you, they're perfect, stronger, faster, smarter, wiser, just <i>everything</i>. of course they'll also show you what you look like at your worst, broken, pitiful, some even say that they've seen themselves as a darkspawn, not Dethroned, <i>darkspawn</i>.<br /> <br /> Then you meet them when he's 'not on the job' and she's barely holding it together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11724-backtoback","name":"backtoback","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T09:23:04-07:00","id":996112,"title":"","content":"96) Someone is gathering Supernaturals (a throng of Prometheans, a small krewe of Sin-Eaters and a few Mages to be exact) to strike against a particularly powerful Arisen. This will lead to turmoil and upset the Infrastructure, so the Unchained and Kindred try to start a counter-measure.<br /> When your group meets this &quot;Someone&quot;, they are left even more confused: he is apparently a Mage, since the Mages present (Mysterium) consider him one of their own. Also, he has a Geist. The vibe you get is more the one of a Kerberoi than that of a Sin-Eater, however (if you can sense such things). And while Geist and Bound are partly-one, this one is infused with his Geist so much you could think there is nothing else there. And to top it all off, for some reason, the Prometheans like him and can interact with him just fine.<br /> To stop this 'war', you will have to find out who or what he is, why he wants to annihilate one of the Arisen and how he became what he is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T11:20:25-07:00","id":996706,"title":"","content":"97: (Hunter/Leviathan) One of the Vigil's big players had some kind of secret research lab on the coast, and thanks to some real Umbrella Corporation stupidity something escaped. Whatever it is, it's hungry and looking to make more of itself. The local leviathans and hunters have always been at a cross-purpose for obvious reasons, but now isn't the time to squabble anymore. Not when swimmers keep disappearing and the state police are getting worried about the negative press. Any killing is gonna have to wait until the fighting is done with this thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T23:20:08-08:00","id":1010529,"title":"","content":"Just because we're almost finished at least one of these threads.<br /> <br /> <b>98: </b>(Genius/Princess) One particularly clever Alhambran operation has decided that they need a way to harvest massive amounts of hope to ensure their city continues to survive. To that end, they've contracted out with an illuminated genius, promising him all the support he needs in return for giving them as much of the hope he harvests as they can bring back. Of course, local princesses <i>and</i> moral geniuses would take at least one or two issues with this situation. So what does happen when the earthly symbols of inspiration fight alongside living symbols of hope?<br /> <br /> <b>99:</b> (Vampire/Promethean) A member of the Ordo Dracul is making waves. He's claiming that there are other ways to make childer, that don't involve turning anyone in the street. Unfortunately, his failures have escaped, and his only success is reportedly making trouble in the local area. The dragon has become consumed by perfecting his creations, and in doing so has alienated much of the local court and annoyed the local prince. Meanwhile, a throng has arrived at the will of the Principle, telling anyone in the know that they've been sent to stop a disaster in the making. It doesn't take a genius to put two and two together on this one, but for vampires nothing is ever so easy. What's the real hidden game under the smokescreen of reviving the dead?<br /> <br /> <b>100: </b>(Werewolf/Mummy) An ancient spirit has returned from the distant reaches of the Shadow that only the oldest werewolves can remember. The spirit is one of conquest, and it's set up shop with a local militia group. Fortunately, there is one person who might known something about it. That person being the ancient undead priest-lord that leads their own cult in the county seat. Said ancient priest-lord has only just been woken up by their cult due to the fact that they alerted their followers to alert them the second such an ancient enemy returned to the world of the living. Surely, focused on the same target, the werewolves and living dead can leave the scene intact?<br /> <br /> <b>101:</b> (<i>Everything</i>) Something is waking up under Yellowstone National Park. A recent spate of heavy seismic activity coupled with a sudden shift in several paranormal communities in the area can only mean that the &quot;supervolcano&quot; is something much worse. World ending worse. Practically anyone who can has sent someone to stop whatever is underneath the caldera from waking up, but everyone has a different way to do it. Werewolves and hunters argue over human sacrifices. Princesses and changelings skirmish over how to treat anyone in the area who <i>doesn't</i> know what's happening. Vampires are trying to claim wells of esoteric power from mages. Sin-Eaters...well, okay, they're pretty much the only ones who are trying to enjoy themselves, much to the annoyance of practically everyone there. The best guess is there's one full month until it does wake up. The real question is, can the various factions lay aside their differences long enough to focus on the end of the world? And if they can't, what will they do when whatever is under the ground is finally awake?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T14:34:14-08:00","id":1017802,"title":"","content":"(Changeling/Your Choice): <br /> <br /> (Non-Changeling perspective): People are being replaced with clones that have all the memories that they're supposed to have, but they've got some nice shiny new powers. Nobody would've noticed... except supernatural creatures are being replaced too, and they're coming back human. Somebodies gotta figure out what's going on and who's behind it. Especially because some of these clones seem to be up to something big...<br /> <br /> (Changeling perspective): There are fetches everywhere, and more pop up by the day. The local freeholds can't keep up with the sudden influx, on top of desperately trying to fend off the Fae incursions and kidnappings that must be happening. And these fetches seem more organized than normal...<br /> <br /> (I'm currently running this campaign, but where the main antagonists have found out how to make their own artificial fetches, and are using them to build a sacred-geometric sigil over the town. It's a cross between invasion of the body snatchers and fullmetal alchemist)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/33282-101-crossover-story-hooks?p=1010529#post1010529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>101:</b> (<i>Everything</i>) Something is waking up under Yellowstone National Park. A recent spate of heavy seismic activity coupled with a sudden shift in several paranormal communities in the area can only mean that the &quot;supervolcano&quot; is something much worse. World ending worse. Practically anyone who can has sent someone to stop whatever is underneath the caldera from waking up, but everyone has a different way to do it. Werewolves and hunters argue over human sacrifices. Princesses and changelings skirmish over how to treat anyone in the area who <i>doesn't</i> know what's happening. Vampires are trying to claim wells of esoteric power from mages. Sin-Eaters...well, okay, they're pretty much the only ones who are trying to enjoy themselves, much to the annoyance of practically everyone there. The best guess is there's one full month until it does wake up. The real question is, can the various factions lay aside their differences long enough to focus on the end of the world? And if they can't, what will they do when whatever is under the ground is finally awake?</div> </div> </div> </div>I ran this with the Cthulhu supplement, and the goal was to prevent the awakening of Azathoth. It was really fun, especially with the Hunters and Vampires really not working together (we had a Cainite in play...)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12771-revanreborn","name":"RevanReborn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12771_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T12:07:40-07:00","id":1381957,"title":"","content":"<b>103:</b> (Beast/Princess) One of the PCs realises/discovers/learns that their Friend with Benefits/Girlfriend/Boyfriend/Spouse/Fianc\u00e9e/Husband/Wife/Romantic Significant Other is a Beast/Noble (depending on wether the PC is a Noble or a Begotten respectively). Said significant other is also extremely powerful (absolute minimum of 7 in Lair/Inner Light) and has both an expansive set of powers and a sizeable power-base. What does the PC do with this info? Will they inform their Nakama/Brood? And is this the prelude to all out war between the two supernatural races, or a strange form of Unity?<br /> <br /> <b>104:</b> (Dragon Rekindled/Princess) News reaches the PC Troupe of a wedding. And not just any wedding; one between a powerful Dragon (Heartstring 9 or 10 and access to all Ablutions and Purviews (and subsequent Impositions)) and one of the Radiant Queens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":25791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","user":"TerrorCooper","date":". 06-29-2020, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T18:13:59-07:00","id":1382646,"title":"","content":"Hey, just a word of warning: the King of Constellations is canonically married. And the King of Crosses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24679-fanguy59","name":"fanguy59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T04:22:53-07:00","id":1382710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fanguy59</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/33282-101-crossover-story-hooks?p=1382646#post1382646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, just a word of warning: the King of Constellations is canonically married. And the King of Crosses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies, I haven\u2019t read much of either Court, so I was unaware of that fact. I\u2019ll just remove it. But still, ST discretion does factor in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T15:46:03-07:00","id":1385144,"title":"","content":"105 (Mummy+Promethean): A meret &amp; a throng meet in a museum. The meret is there to &quot;acquire&quot; some Iremite relics that should not be in human hands. The throng is there to kill some pandorans that are part of a popular exhibit.<br /> Then, screaming. People running. The pandorans have woken up &amp; have consumed the relics, acquiring the power that was held within. The pandorans now can only be killed by a mixture of Promethean &amp; Arisen energies.<br /> Time to get creative.<br /> \u25cf Alternatively, some Amkhata awaken at the same time as the pandorans. The point is the meret &amp; the throng are forced to work together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T19:13:09-07:00","id":1387392,"title":"","content":"<b>106:</b> (Siren: The Drowning + Princess): A close friend of one, or more, of the PCs and their Girlfriend/Boyfriend (depends on which side of the nest the chosen friend swings towards and ST fiat) announces to the Clique/Nakama that they\u2019re getting married, and the lucky couple want the PCs to help set it all up. Naturally, things start getting screwy when the Siren\u2019s friends also start helping out, whilst enemies from both sides attempt to avert, ruin or at least crash, the wedding. (Note that this can also be done from the Siren\u2019s side of things)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T03:15:59-07:00","id":1388873,"title":"","content":"Came up with these while reading the 1.1 edition of the Genius: The Transgression rulebook just now.<br /> <br /> <b>107:</b> (Genius + Leviathan) In an attempt to get Earth's Most Wicked under control without resorting to the usage of the Baraqu, the Marduk Society have started hiring Genii to directly combat Leviathans in Apotheosis (after luring them away from major population centres). The players can be either the Collaboration of Inspired who were hired, or a Cohort of Leviathans sent to nip this new project in the bud (or who were just foul-lucked enough to be the team's first actual targets). Time for some good old Mech Vs. Kaiju Brawls!<br /> <br /> <b>108:</b> (Genius + Princess) After learning of the Court of Tears, their Modus Operandi and the general(-ish) location of Alahambra within the Darkness, a Collaboration of high Inspiration (7-10), high Obligation/Enlightenment (7-10) Inspired have decided to wage the same sort of war upon The Last Empress and her Witches that the Peerage waged upon Lemuria, and have started gathering supporters, both Genii and Noble. Will the PC Nakama/Clique/Collaboration join in, or try and put a stop to this whole thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":25791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","user":"TerrorCooper","date":". 06-19-2021, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T02:48:00-07:00","id":1396634,"title":"","content":"<b>109:</b> (Hunter/Beast, Demon, Dragon, Leviathan, etc whatever works best)<br /> <br /> Hunter POV: You, and the rest of your Cell, have managed to chase/track a particularly large, and powerful, monster out into the countryside. Now the main problem is finding it and putting it six (6) feet under before it can either successfully escape or kill the lot of you. Unfortunately, it seems to have just drained some sort of supernatural energy well, so things just got a lot more complicated.<br /> <br /> \u2018Monster\u2019 POV: You\u2019ve been running from these fella\u2019s for several days now, and you\u2019ve been running on fumes, as far as the juju needed to fuel your powers is a concern. Fortunately, you\u2019ve, albeit barely, managed to top-up from the dregs of a well of said energies. Now, let\u2019s see what you can do about those blasted hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":25791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","user":"TerrorCooper","date":". 06-29-2020, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T09:43:16-07:00","id":1399863,"title":"","content":"110.<b>Mummy/Werewolf</b><br /> Something has gone VERY wrong in [Fill-In-The-Blank's werewolf pack's] territory, as undead and seemingly unkillable aberrations appear out of nowhere. Deformed, cancerous and maddened from constant agony, these malformed devils warp and corrupt everything they touch simply by existing.<br /> <br /> How can the pack defeat something that literally never dies? And what about this ebon-skinned Star Pharaoh---clearly a godlike Claimed---that's shown up looking for these unkillable abominations? Is he friend or foe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-14T15:38:13-08:00","id":1432257,"title":"","content":"<b>111:</b> (Beast/Leviathan/Mummy/Princess/Vampire)<br /> <br /> For millennia, five (5) individuals, a Begotten, a Leviathan, a Noble, an Arisen, and a member of the Kindred, have been keeping the peace between their respective races, and becoming best friends (to the point of considering themselves siblings) in the process. One day, one of them is kidnapped by an unknown group for unknown, but surely dastardly, designs. It's now up to the other four to rescue their friend, hopefully before anyone else finds out and decides to use this spread chaos, or (even worse) to ignite war!<br /> <br /> <b>112:</b> (Beast/Princess)<br /> <br /> Rumors are beginning to circulate in the Begotten and Noble communities of a Beast and an Enlightened getting together as a couple. A small team (the PCs) is called forth to investigate these rumors, and learn of the veracity behind them. No matter if they're correct or not, the team is to find the two and learn just what is actually going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":25791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","user":"TerrorCooper","date":". 01-14-2021, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T15:30:04-07:00","id":1452383,"title":"","content":"I've no idea where this came from, but it most likely has something to do with the various character ideas spinning around in my head..<br /> <br /> <b>113:</b> (Core/All) The PC Troupe have just stumbled upon a most peculiar find; a mortal able to sense the flow of supernatural energies without aid. And not only do they sense the usage of said energies, but also their gathering and storage, places of power (Avernian Gates, paths into the Hedge, Chambers, Arisen Tombs and so on), items imbued with power that doesn't follow the more mundane rules of the universe (Gadgets, Relics, Azothic Items, Fetishes, etc), the flow of said energies in their 'natural' state (Essence 'radiating' off of damn-near everything, Vitae circulating inside of both themselves and others, Glamour coiling in the air around those feeling intense emotions, the 'pooling' of Aether run-off from Infrastructure) <i>and</i> the presence of supernatural beings and creatures. All attempts to analyze this fellow turn up the same; they're nothing more than a mortal who just so happens to be extremely sensitive to the supernatural.<br /> <br /> What does the group make of this discovery? Should they kill this innocent person (who's been minding their own business whilst dealing with all the phenomenon going on around them) before they become a threat? Or try to convert them to the Troupe's cause? Or maybe something else...<br /> <br /> OOC: The Mortal is genuinely just that; a mortal. They just so happen to possess every possible variation of the 'Unseen Sense' Merit as warranted by the game-lines present (yes, even the stuff from Fan-Lines, if they're included).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T17:45:23-07:00","id":1466070,"title":"","content":"114 (Hunter/any other gameline) A cell of hunters &amp; a coterie/pack/motley/krewe/brood/etc. attack each other, when the area around you both collapses. Quickly, the two groups come to the conclusion that this was an attack upon both of you.<br /> The enemy of my enemy is my friend, anyone? Or is there too much bad blood between you for such a situation to work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T17:46:31-07:00","id":1466071,"title":"","content":"115 (Demon+Princess): You &amp; some fellow Unchained have uncovered a plot of the God-Machine. It has confirmed the existence of some kind of magic-user called &quot;Nobles&quot;, however is having trouble uncovering important details. A piece of specialized Infrastructure has been constructed to acquire some of those details. Now all that's needed is for a Noble to be hooked up the device.<br /> Screw up the God-Machine's plans here &amp; you could get some valuable allies. But you're on a clock &amp; the angels are closing in on a suspected Noble. Tick tock tick tock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-20T05:28:52-07:00","id":1522823,"title":"","content":"116(Promethean/Demon)<br /> <br /> A Promethean throng catch word that a Promethean has been taken by a Cult which seems to be experimenting in them. At the same time a Demon ring is aware of a special piece of infrastructure which the God-machine is working on. Both end up investigating the same Cult/infrastructure at the same time.<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> (The kidnapped Promethean is the linchpin to this occult matrix, and really you don't want to find out what the God-machine will do with this alchemical power).</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 117 (Demon/Mummy) While investigating what the God-machine is, some rumours lead your ring to a Cult worshipping some ancient being/God-like entity that supposedly has access to Occult powers similar to the God-machine's, maybe they can be used against it? But maybe the Cult is another front for the God-machine.<br /> <br /> The Meret has uncovered some records of an Iremite plan to create a giant machine, something to alter the world in such a way as to seal the judges off from Duat? Perhaps it is still out there, if they can find it? Of course the Judges will want it destroyed, or disabled, while the Mummy's might prefer to take control of it. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> In this story, the answer to &quot;what is the God-machine?&quot; Is an Iremite device to thwart the Judges.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> With Demons infiltrating the Cult and Mummy infiltrating the God-machine, who will get what they want in the end?<br /> <br /> 118 (Promethean/Mummy)<br /> <br /> A Promethean trying to figure out how to be human, a Mummy trying to remember what it meant to be human, crossing paths as both are driven to seek the same thing. An object has appeared, maybe a Relic or maybe an Azothic object, it seems to have some odd properties. People are drawn towards it and report various miracles upon touching it. As a result a small Cult has formed around it which attracts the attention of the Mummy's Cult, while the Azothic Radience attracts Prometheans.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Both Sekhem (refined Dedwen) and Azoth (refined Pyros) are in some sense life forces, maybe two sides of the same coin, maybe not, but an Artifact which contains both Sekhem and Azoth would have some very strange properties...</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ps: working on a setting hack for mummy/demon/Promethean crossover game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-24T13:49:35-07:00","id":1523098,"title":"","content":"<b>117</b> <br /> A surprising number of the supernaturally-inclined enjoy illegal underground combat sports. Sometimes they get something out of it, like blood, glory, or Glamour. Sometimes they're looking to recruit. Sometimes they just like the vibe.<br /> Whatever their motive, illegal pit fights draw a diverse supernatural crowd and they often develop their own strange culture unique to the scene, depending on who participates.<br /> The most common rule is simply not to unduly hurt the regular folks who make up most of the competitors, and using supernatural powers against them is seen as poor sportsmanship. Since the sort of people willing to step into an underground bloodsport tournament are often in demand from a variety of cults and other clandestine groups, there's often some set of (often complicated) rules about who can be approached for recruitment or less wholesome reasons, and ways to mark people to prevent poaching.<br /> Naturally, there are more than a few supernatural denizens who think throwing down with a werewolf or stepping up to a literal ogre sounds like a fun night out, but these sorts of matches have their own rules in different, more secluded arenas with a <i>very</i> exclusive viewership. Sometimes this is purely for amusement or individual bragging rights, but in some places it develops into a full-on system of dueling, where monsters can send champions to settle disputes that go beyond their normal political spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-17T21:48:22-07:00","id":1524212,"title":"","content":"120 (Changeling/Hunter/any*)<br /> Many of the workers at the Office of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Director_of_National_Intelligence\" target=\"_blank\">the Director of National Intelligence </a>are a bit...off, all of the sudden. Some have picked up new tics, others have started spontaneously exhibiting symptoms of everything from Anhedonia to various personality disorders. A few, to the increasing alarm of the American Government, exhibit patterns of behavior that seem completely inhuman. Of course, that's because they are inhuman. More specifically, they're all fetches. Is this the beginning of a ploy to take over the country? The unfortunate consequence of some sort of Arcadian fad for bureaucracy? Part of a scheme by darker powers yet?<br /> <br /> Whatever the reason, the American government wants (depending on which parts of it you're talking to) answers, a way to stop the apparent incursion, bloody and painful revenge on those responsible, or to sweep all this under the rug so things can go back to business as usual. The Barret Commission and TF:V are torn by the contradictory demands of a panicking national security establishment, while others in the government start wading into the Vigil in a bid to protect themselves or makes sense of the situation. Changelings, for their part, have the opportunity to make an unlikely and powerful ally-If they can prove their worth, and avoid being smothered under the ensuing fallout.<br /> *Other supernaturals may be drawn in too, either due to a preexisting investment in the workings of the federal government, or simply because whoever is calling the shots can't actually tell a Fairest from a Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27692-alexanderalaska","name":"alexanderalaska","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T18:01:09-08:00","id":1528466,"title":"","content":"#121 - GMC/Changeling<br /> <br /> Your group, whether they be Angels on a mission or regular humans unknowingly doing the God Machine\u2019s will, finds a nearby piece of Infrastructure is glitching out. This particular piece of Infrastructure has been taken over by a portion of The Hedge that has somehow infiltrated the perfect world built by the God Machine. No one other than your group has noticed this \u2014 nor do they notice that during these glitches someone wanders, or gets led, into The Hedge. After watching this malfunctioning Infrastructure your group finds that some of those who\u2019ve went into The Hedge come back out. For all intents and purposes they look &amp; act the same as they did prior to entering The Hedge. Over time it becomes clear that True Fae are only taking Clockwork Servitors &amp; humans who have been similarly altered with clockwork machinery to be the perfect pieces of Infrastructure necessary for its plans. The God Machine does not offer any guidance on what to do to remedy the situation because this is <b><i>not</i></b> supposed to happen. Ever. Do you look for answers within the safety of other Infrastructure or do you risk entering The Hedge to find out more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27935-trynmybest","name":"trynmybest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27935_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T22:09:42-08:00","id":1528473,"title":"","content":"#122 Forsaken / Sin Eaters<br /> <br /> A spirit of formidable power has arrived on the scene and started taking over the local court. Meanwhile a being in the local underworld with the same name has also began making moves. Are these beings the same creature? If not why do they have the same name? Are they coordinating their actions across multiple worlds? Are the Shadow and the Underworld the only words they have designs on?<br /> <br /> 122+1 Requiem / Forsaken<br /> <br /> A member of the strix has become a magath (or if started as a spirit and became a strix magath after). How did this happen? Is this some hitherto unknown Idigam? Have the Pure teamed up with a member of the Seven? Are cats and dogs living together in harmony?<br /> <br /> 122+2 Forsaken / Demon<br /> <br /> What happens when a demon's cover becomes one of the claimed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","user":"ShadowcatX","date":".  Weird linking happening 01-13-2024, 01:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T08:16:15-07:00","id":1543263,"title":"","content":"<b>123:</b> (Werewolf/Promethean) A Throng of Prometheans have recently been created, an extremely rare confluence of events leading to Created of different Lineages arising within relatively close proximity to one another. A Spirit, for reasons unknown to even itself, is formed by the sheer volume of essence aligned to the new beings, and decides to join them both out of gratitude for inadvertently creating it, and a desire to continue existing.<br /> Cue road trip as this madcap group meanders across the world trying to figure out this whole 'existing' thing, trying to survive hostile Spirits, Werewolves, Sublimati, Pandorans and Alchemists, and attempting to become human/a Spirit of Humanity.<br /> <br /> <b>124:</b> (Princess/Storyteller's Choice) The Troupe comes to be attached to a Noble, enjoying a wonderful life that's difficult to find in this World of Darkness... Until the Noble's magic starts to go out of control, the Enlightened them-self eventually falling into despair, before finally transforming into a monster in a veritable conflagration of tragedy and sorrow. Eventually a group of other Nobles arrive, see the commotion and explain what's happened; the Noble the PC's knew was a member of the Court of Petals. The PCs, upon learning the deal of this Court and its supposed 'Queen' immediately swear vengeance, and set out to avenge their friend/the little one all Kratos-Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-10T15:31:15-08:00","id":1556441,"title":"","content":"<b>125:</b> (Hunter/Changeling/Beast/Any(/All)) For one reason or another, a particularly skilled and powerful Practitioner-Sorcerer of both the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/475-wyrd-sorcery\">Wyrd</a> <i>and</i> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/864954-primordial-sorcery-homebrew\">Primordial</a> varieties has taken offence to the Cell\u2019s activities, and laid down a curse on them, trapping them all in a constant cycle through the various supernatural races. How are the PCs supposed to get out of this one, and what did that damned Sorcerer mean by the spell only ending when they learn to \u2018look through another\u2019s eyes\u2019?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}